<section class="section tint" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2>From signed agreement to a clean file</h2>
      <p>Three moves, repeated per round. Nothing is mailed until the evidence supports it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step-cell">
        <span class="step-num">1</span>
        <h3>Review and prepare</h3>
        <p>Intake captures the client, the reports and the identity documents. Each bureau's tradelines are entered once, scored, and matched to a theory — not my account, duplicate collection, paid by insurance, impermissible inquiry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-cell">
        <span class="step-num">2</span>
        <h3>Dispute and mail</h3>
        <p>Clearpath drafts the letter with the relevant FCRA section, the account identifiers and the evidence list. Approve it, and the mailroom groups letters by client and bureau, prints the labels, and records the certified tracking.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step-cell">
        <span class="step-num">3</span>
        <h3>Respond and escalate</h3>
        <p>The response clock is visible on every open dispute. Verified, deleted, no reply — each outcome sets the next round. Escalations to the CFPB or state regulator keep the same case history attached.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

