<section class="section tint" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2>The things agencies ask first</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Is Clearpath a credit repair company?</summary>
        <div class="answer">No. Clearpath is the software Denovo Credit built to run its own practice, and it is licensed to other agencies. Denovo Credit is the credit repair organization; the platform is the tool.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you guarantee deletions or score increases?</summary>
        <div class="answer">Never. Outcomes depend on the furnisher and the bureau. What Clearpath guarantees is process: every dispute is evidence-backed, mailed on time, tracked to its response deadline and recorded in an audit log.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can our clients see their own file?</summary>
        <div class="answer">Yes. Each client gets portal credentials scoped to their own record: three bureau scores, dispute status, document requests and a message thread with your team. The portal carries your brand, your colours and, on Network, your domain.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where does the data live?</summary>
        <div class="answer">Clearpath ships as a container with a SQLite database and a document directory on a persistent volume. You run it in your own cloud account, so your client data never leaves your infrastructure. The schema is plain SQL and portable.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do letters and labels get printed?</summary>
        <div class="answer">The mailroom groups approved letters by client and bureau, then generates a PDF packet: one letter per page with the recipient block, plus a label sheet and a manifest page. Print duplex or single-sided — the packet is laid out for both.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What about CFPB or state escalations?</summary>
        <div class="answer">Escalation is a dispute status, so the evidence, the mail history and the original letter stay attached. Mark a dispute escalated and Clearpath records the change, the actor and the timestamp in the audit chain.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#9db4d6">Denovo Credit</span>
        <h2 style="margin-top:12px">See Clearpath on your own caseload</h2>
        <p>
          A 30-minute walkthrough: we load three of your accounts, draft the letters, and show you the packet
          and the client view. No slide deck.
        </p>
        <% if (query.sent === "1") { %>
          <div class="notice notice-ok" style="margin-top:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.1);border-color:#2f4a6b;color:#e7f0fb">
            <svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <div>Thanks — your request is in. We reply from <strong><%= tenant && tenant.support_email ? tenant.support_email : 'hello@denovocredit.com' %></strong> within one business day.</div>
          </div>
        <% } else { %>
          <% if (query.sent === "0") { %>
            <div class="notice notice-error" style="margin-top:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.1);border-color:#5d3040;color:#ffdbe4">
              <svg><use href="#i-alert"/></svg>
              <div>We need your name and a valid work email to reply. Try again below.</div>
            </div>
          <% } %>
          <form class="contact-form" method="post" action="/contact" novalidate>
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
            <div><label class="sr-only" for="c-name">Your name</label><input class="input" id="c-name" name="name" placeholder="Your name" required maxlength="80"></div>
            <div><label class="sr-only" for="c-email">Work email</label><input class="input" id="c-email" name="email" type="email" placeholder="Work email" required maxlength="120"></div>
            <div><label class="sr-only" for="c-agency">Agency</label><input class="input" id="c-agency" name="agency" placeholder="Agency name" maxlength="120"></div>
            <div>
              <label class="sr-only" for="c-size">Active clients</label>
              <select class="select" id="c-size" name="size">
                <option value="">Active clients…</option>
                <option>1–40</option>
                <option>41–150</option>
                <option>151–400</option>
                <option>400+</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div class="span-2">
              <label class="sr-only" for="c-msg">What do you want to fix?</label>
              <textarea class="textarea" id="c-msg" name="message" rows="3" maxlength="1000" placeholder="What is slowing your team down today?"></textarea>
            </div>
            <div class="span-2">
              <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" type="submit">Request a walkthrough</button>
              <p class="tiny" style="color:#93a5c0;margin-top:10px">
                We use this only to reply. No newsletter, no list rental.
              </p>
            </div>
          </form>
        <% } %>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
